WEBVTT

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:23.040
Okay, okay, keep back!
It's dangerous here!

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.510
Word is that one of Holmes's experiments
failed, and he blew up his flat.

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:30.220
He says he will offer everyone a free
consultation to make up for it,

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.220
but for right now, he wants you to leave.

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:21.500
The Lord of Crime?

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:25.080
A Scandal in the British Empire Act 3

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.330
Miss Adler isn't dealing
with the government,

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.790
but the Lord of Crime?

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:28.170
Are you certain, Sherlock?

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:35.300
Hey! He's a killer! I find it very hard to
believe that he will keep his promises!

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:37.890
Are you sure we should just let
Miss Adler go off like this?

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:42.850
Hey, say something! Hey, Sherlock!

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:42.850
No, not that... There's no
sure-fire way to save her...

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:44.390
But...

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:46.270
Ah, damn it!

00:02:46.270 --> 00:02:50.690
Damn it! There must be something else,
right?! Then let's have it!

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:54.780
Sherlock...

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:56.280
It's hopeless.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.740
No matter how much I think it through,
I always arrive at the same conclusion.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:03.080
This is the worst-case plan,
but right now, we have nothing else.

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.170
Miss Adler...

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:16.260
I know it hasn't been very long,
but thank you so much for everything.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:20.010
I'd have liked to enjoy a nice,
long chat over some tea.

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:22.720
Thank you, Miss Hudson.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.060
This is goodbye for good, isn't it?

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:32.320
Oh, Sherly, are you going to miss me
that much when I'm gone?

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:34.190
I'm sorry to hear that.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:36.950
Ha, the old tough-girl act.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:40.410
Irene!

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:46.540
You're sure this deal is going
to warrant your life, right?

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:51.130
Of course. I may have
messed things up a bit,

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:54.920
but I finally found the right conditions
to turn things around.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:58.680
She's bluffing. She's going into
this expecting to be killed.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:01.550
I see. That's a relief.

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:05.520
It was her mistake to steal
something so pernicious.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:09.390
But there is nothing at all
false about her desire

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:12.110
to make the world a better place.

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:17.740
I have to... keep her safe,
no matter what!

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:29.040
Do you think Sherlock Holmes
will be coming, William?

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:34.840
Yes. He will definitely show up.
For Irene Adler's sake.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:37.710
He is not interested in
the document itself.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:42.680
His first thought will likely be
to safeguard Miss Adler's life,

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:46.930
so he will not try too hard
to uncover our identities.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:50.600
But to put it another way,
unless Holmes receives a sure guarantee

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.860
that Adler's life will be spared,

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:56.150
there is no way that he
will back down, is there?

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:59.530
We'll be looking to you
again on this one, Will.

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:00.990
Yes...

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.780
I have a plan.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:28.060
Miss Irene Adler, I presume?

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:32.020
The gentleman has already arrived.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:34.310
In there, please.

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:48.200
Welcome, Irene Adler.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:58.170
I brought the papers. But please
permit me to verify one thing.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:04.050
Your reforms to better the world--
you mean no deceit in what you say, yes?

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:09.720
Of course not. Our objectives are
the same. If you feel they are not,

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:13.730
then you are free at that
moment to accuse me.

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:15.650
Very well.

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:20.400
All right, then as a token of your
loyalty, hand over the document.

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:32.000
Not yet. You can't turn it over yet.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.000
Sherlock!

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:40.000
So, you've come after all,
Sherlock Holmes.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.970
We meet at last, Lord of Crime.

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:45.510
Sherlock, what are you doing here?

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:48.050
Huh? Keeping you safe.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:49.430
Me?

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:52.060
And it's not just me...!

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:01.360
The Yard?!

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:04.070
There is nowhere for you to run...

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:06.530
...Lord of Crime.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:08.450
You'll be killed, too!

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:13.080
Take it easy, Irene.
Let me handle this, all right?

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:15.210
Sherlock...

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:19.540
Are you planning to arrest me?

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:22.630
That all depends on you.

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:24.300
I'm listening.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.680
Now that I've learnt
what is in these papers,

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:31.220
my first thought was how I could
make sure to protect Irene.

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:33.470
As long as it is possible that
she might leak the contents,

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.770
then regardless of what
happens with these papers,

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:38.350
the government is going
to try to eliminate her.

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:42.400
Which means that about all I can do
is get her out of the country,

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.030
but there remains some doubt
as to the certitude of that plan.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:48.570
So what exactly can I do to
completely ensure her safety?

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:51.660
It's to have her be protected by someone
in the underworld of London,

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:57.500
someone who is able to freely
carry out his own plans.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:02.090
<i>You</i>, Lord of Crime.
Only you can protect Irene.

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:06.130
I hate to admit this, but you are
the <i>only </i>one who can protect her!

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:14.390
Indeed. As I've already told her,
I will keep her alive.

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:16.850
This is an incontrovertible fact,

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:20.810
but it will take more than
my word to convince you.

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:32.320
Irene Adler, write my name on here, seal
it in the envelope, then give it to him.

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:36.950
Holmes, if ever you
determine that she is dead,

00:08:36.950 --> 00:08:41.500
you are free to open the envelope,
read the name, and then come to me.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:46.340
I will place my trust in you,
too, Sherlock Holmes.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.800
All right.

00:08:58.520 --> 00:09:00.140
It's written.

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:05.480
I have it in hand.

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:12.740
This concludes our business.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:15.580
You may leave, along with
your dilettante police force.

00:09:15.580 --> 00:09:16.540
Huh?

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:18.500
Tch, you knew?

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:23.290
Now, if you'll excuse me,
Sherlock Holmes...

00:09:33.220 --> 00:09:36.510
It looks like he's given us time
to say our goodbyes.

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:40.020
Thanks so much for going
to such lengths for me

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:41.770
after only knowing me
for such a brief time.

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:43.600
I'll tell John you said so, too.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:49.230
I've done nothing but lie to you,
so I doubt you'll take my word for this,

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:52.700
but I am rather fond of you.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:57.790
Heh, that's a lie.

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:00.120
No, it's the truth.

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:05.960
Don't forget about me, all right?

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:10.590
I couldn't forget you if I wanted to.

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:14.220
Farewell, my detective.

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:29.980
As long as you're alive, we'll run
into each other again somewhere.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:42.410
There's a passageway like
this beneath the church?

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:54.880
Holmes came after all, but we concluded
our transaction without incident.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:57.430
Thanks to your plan, Will.

00:10:57.430 --> 00:10:59.430
Good to hear, Brother.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:03.810
Does this mean that they were
anticipating Sherlock's interference?

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:07.650
Is it possible--no,
there's no doubt about it...

00:11:07.650 --> 00:11:12.150
The Lord of Crime does not
refer to just one person.

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:15.030
And the heart of this organisation...

00:11:19.370 --> 00:11:22.870
My life is now in your hands.

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:28.170
In return for your loyalty,
I will give you what you wish.

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:32.840
Come, look up at me, Irene Adler.

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:36.430
Let us make our way toward
the final negotiation together.

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:59.700
I thought... that you were
a smarter man than this.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:10.330
You recovered the document
and liquidated Adler.

00:12:10.330 --> 00:12:13.340
At least, that's what was
written in your telegram.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:17.050
I trust there's an explanation for this?

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:22.760
The contents were extremely fascinating--

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:28.230
how the French Revolution was a
social experiment set up by Britain.

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:32.770
And how the master of the plot,
Maximilien Robespierre,

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:38.450
was the author of this document,
and an agent working for Britain.

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:41.570
Yes, it is the strategy that
the British Empire used

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:46.330
in their effort to bring about
the French Revolution.

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:49.750
If these papers ever became public,

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:54.250
our allied nations would have
ample and justifiable reason

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:57.050
to go to war against Britain.

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:06.010
My only interest is this--whether or
not you are an enemy of Britain.

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:09.850
I have but a single demand.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:12.060
Your silence.

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:17.030
From the time of my youth,

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:20.780
I have been active in exposing the
corruption and misdeeds of the nobility

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:23.740
in an effort to collapse the class system.

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:29.580
In other words, you are the "Lord of
Crime" that everyone is talking about?

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:35.590
Yes. Everything that has transpired
has been part of our plan.

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:38.880
We, who are "James Moriarty."

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:41.380
From my internal investigation,

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:44.680
I knew that you had someone
outstanding collaborating with you.

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:46.850
I believe you are...

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:49.930
I am William, Director Holmes.

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:54.310
I see. The Lord of Crime
and his consultants.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:58.360
Our objective is the same as
the author of these papers--

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:02.030
to bring about liberty
and equality in this land.

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:06.490
The leader of the French Revolution
was Maximilien Robespierre.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:09.620
Following the execution of King Louis XVI,

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.460
he abruptly preached for the
necessity of the Reign of Terror

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:14.710
and carried out the purge.

00:14:16.710 --> 00:14:20.760
He has been cast as one of the
villains of the French Revolution.

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:23.840
His actions are difficult to comprehend
through conventional thinking.

00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:27.350
However, there was a reason behind them.

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:30.140
That being to overthrow the monarchy

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:33.520
and make the country
centred around its citizens.

00:14:34.980 --> 00:14:39.230
He executed the king, and the
revolution appeared to be successful.

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:42.990
However... as a result of his
agitating for the ruling class

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:45.360
as being the cause of their evils,

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:48.330
the people clamoured for the
nobility to be killed, as well,

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:51.500
and the situation spun out of his control.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:55.620
It was then that he decided
to adopt a certain measure...

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:00.250
That being the Reign of Terror.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:04.260
The aristocrats and citizens
who opposed the revolution

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:06.590
were executed, one after another.

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:12.430
It was through the Terror that he
switched the public's attention

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:15.390
from the nobility onto himself...

00:15:16.900 --> 00:15:20.230
And by creating a common
enemy for both sides...

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:28.570
...he put an end to the affair
with his own death.

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:36.580
Yes, and what we are trying
to do is the same thing.

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:44.170
Our goal is to divide the power
as close to equally as is possible.

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:47.380
By employing the means
of crime to that end,

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:50.640
we become the common "evil" shared
by both the nobility and the people,

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:53.890
urging both sides to join hand in hand.

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:57.390
Our end will be the same as his--

00:15:57.390 --> 00:16:02.820
the elimination of the "heinous
Moriartys," which were of our own making.

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:08.110
That is our plan.

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:11.700
I have no intention of denying
your sense of patriotism

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:13.910
in attempting to sacrifice yourselves.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:19.040
That is, however, assuming that
you three really <i>are </i>patriots.

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:23.840
If I decide that you are out of control,
then as enemies of Britain...

00:16:23.840 --> 00:16:27.720
...I will eliminate you.
That is a promise.

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:32.100
We understand. That is the whole reason
why we revealed ourselves to you,

00:16:32.100 --> 00:16:35.270
who are said to be the government itself.

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:41.270
Very well. The British government
promises henceforth

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:43.980
to remain silent toward your activities.

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:46.280
You have our gratitude.

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:51.950
Director Holmes, may I ask one thing?

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:54.620
Why would you continue
to keep this document

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:58.000
and run the risk of it being stolen?

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:01.790
There must be some special reason.

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:04.550
You said it yourself.

00:17:04.550 --> 00:17:07.130
First, Her Majesty feels that
the failure of this mission

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:11.430
is a crime for which Britain must
shoulder the weight forever more.

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:13.430
But there is one other reason.

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:18.480
The true name of Robespierre,
the author of this document...

00:17:18.480 --> 00:17:22.440
...is Sherrinford Holmes.

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:25.320
Ancestor to the Holmes family.

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:29.780
This is the crime and punishment that
our family must continue to bear.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:33.950
It is the reason why I continue to pledge
allegiance to the British Government.

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:39.460
I have not told my brother any of this.

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:43.420
I want him to live free, you understand.

00:17:43.420 --> 00:17:47.250
Now, enough of this excessive talk.

00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:55.970
Our deal is now struck.

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:13.740
How are you feeling, Dr Watson?

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:15.780
Mycroft...

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:17.700
Did you need to see Sherlock?

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:20.330
He appears to have stepped
out at the moment.

00:18:20.330 --> 00:18:23.500
Yes, it is better this way.

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:28.460
My brother has given his all
for a certain woman.

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:31.630
He may have had some
special feelings for her.

00:18:31.630 --> 00:18:36.510
That is why I wanted to come
and tell him about this directly.

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:03.080
Good night, Mr Sherlock Holmes.

00:19:17.850 --> 00:19:19.510
Sherlock...

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:23.810
What's the matter, you two?
You both look like you've seen a ghost.

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:31.230
Actually, um... Mycroft came by
with a message for you.

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:34.240
Word is that Miss Adler has passed away.

00:19:34.240 --> 00:19:37.610
That her body was pulled
out of the Thames.

00:19:50.000 --> 00:19:53.460
If ever you determine that she is dead,

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:58.140
you are free to open the envelope,
read the name, and then come to me.

00:20:28.420 --> 00:20:33.170
She's dead. "That woman" is dead.

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.090
That's the truth, isn't it?

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:49.770
Now, it's time for our last job.

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:57.320
Fred, go and select a body to
stand in for her from the morgue.

00:20:57.320 --> 00:20:59.110
Very well.

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:04.200
Irene, as of today,
as of this moment, you are dead.

00:21:04.200 --> 00:21:06.500
From now on, we are
going to put you to work

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:08.790
as a member of our organisation.

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:10.170
Right.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:14.710
You're going to need a new name.

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:19.380
We will give you our name,
James, as your first name.

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:21.470
For your last name...

00:21:21.470 --> 00:21:24.350
A new life...

00:21:24.350 --> 00:21:25.930
New friends...

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:27.520
Bonds...

00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:03.090
My name is Bonde.

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:05.260
James Bonde.

00:23:44.450 --> 00:23:51.030
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i>:
"The Phantom of Whitechapel Act 1."

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:51.990
The Phantom of Whitechapel Act 1
